{{Dialogue Start}}
<pre>{
	"$type": "RPG.GameCore.ChangeDynamicOptionalBlock",
	"BlockKey": "100"
}</pre>
:{{Black Screen|After some time...}}
:'''March 7th:''' I bet Argenti would think these fireworks were really... beautiful.
:'''March 7th:''' We didn't know him very long, but he was a pretty nice guy.
:'''March 7th:''' ...
:'''March 7th:''' Tsk, I hope he made it...
:'''Pom-Pom:''' The Express managed to escape the crisis, but Pom-Pom still feels a little sad... Pom-Pom wonders what happened to Argenti.
:<!--0.4-second delay-->
:'''March 7th:''' *sigh* Velite just left the Express too &mdash; he looked really upset. I guess he didn't know what Argenti was thinking, either...
:'''Himeko:''' The Knights of Beauty are made up of individuals who are used to traveling through the cosmos alone... they are difficult to understand, and the starry sky is their home. Perhaps this firework show is a symbol of his honor.
:'''March 7th:''' But the fireworks...
:'''Pom-Pom:''' ...And the starry sky...
:'''March 7th:''' ...He didn't see it...
:'''Himeko:''' He has his own goals... and struggles. After all, the Aeon of Beauty has likely already fallen.
:<!--0.3-second delay-->
:'''March 7th:''' Huh? You mean Idrila &mdash; the one he wouldn't stop talking about? But... he said he'd find them... and fulfill his duty to protect them.
:'''Himeko:''' The fact that Idrila has fallen is tacitly acknowledged by some Knights of Beauty. Naturally, there are others who don't want to believe it... like the one you met. He probably thinks that Idrila is simply missing &mdash; hiding somewhere beyond the reach of mortals.
:'''Himeko:''' (Trailblazer), the crisis is over, and our unexpected guest has left, but I think there's still something we should talk about.
:'''Himeko:''' ...In your opinion, what is beauty?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} A lover's eyes.
::'''Himeko:''' They must be beautiful eyes.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} All fun and no work!
::'''Himeko:''' Sounds like a wonderful life &mdash; I'm sure many have dreams of that.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Obsessively watching cats eat food.
::'''Himeko:''' Haha, you have a wild imagination.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} That which exists between the Crew...
::'''Himeko:''' Oh? That's a good answer.
:'''Himeko:''' Beauty takes many forms, and different people have different answers... I wonder what exactly it is that the Knights of Beauty are pursuing through the cosmos.
:'''Himeko:''' Let's assume that Argenti finds the "missing" Idrila. Will he be able to recognize THEM with his human eyes? Or, obsessed with his version of "THEM," will he turn a blind eye and not even see THEM for who THEY are?
:'''March 7th:''' Mm... It did seem like he had a kind of... tunnel vision. And it sounded like he was holding himself to unreachable standards to attain his dreams.
:'''March 7th:''' I didn't quite wrap my head around him... I guess if we're ever back in Belobog and see a red-headed knight shouting into trashcans &mdash; "Idrila, are you in there!? Idrilaaaa!" ...I won't be surprised.
:'''March 7th:''' But, so what? I still think he was a nice guy, even if he was a bit weird...
:'''Pom-Pom:''' *sigh* Where were we supposed to be going again?
